%U A400810 7708282046983,43740428813029,248203929959881,1408426504122061,7992078890577427,45350838163523077
%N A400810 Size of Type C megastars of star triples in the Spectre aperiodic monotile tiling.
%C A400810 The chiral aperiodic Spectre monotile tiling (discovered in 2023) forms hierarchical, fractal macro-structures called clusters of star triples (three Spectre tiles head-on) of five different families, megastars of two types, and palindromes of megastars (see A400812). This sequence gives the number of star triples in successive generations of Type C megastars.
%C A400810 A Type C megastar consists of a minor star triple in the center and three arms, each a cluster of star triples of Family C (A397116) of the previous generation; each such cluster is a chain of Type A palindromes (A400811).
%C A400810 The fractal growth is governed by the limiting constant 5.674473356937... = 1 + 2*sqrt(6)*cos((1/3)*arccos(sqrt(6)/4)), the largest root of x^3 - 3*x^2 - 15*x - 1 = 0, as for the Type A megastars (A397120) and the Type A palindromes (A400811).
%C A400810 The vertex span of the Type C megastar of generation n (the number of star triples on a longest path through it) is Fibonacci(3*n-1) = A015448(n).
%H A400810 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="/A400810/b400810.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..100</a>
%H A400810 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="/A400810/a400810.png">Type C megastar of generation 4 (217 star triples)</a>
%H A400810 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="/A400810/a400810_1.png">Type C megastar of generation 4 with a longest path (vertex span 89 = Fibonacci(11))</a>
%H A400810 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="/A400810/a400810_2.png">All Type C megastars in the level-6 supertile</a>
%H A400810 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="https://zenodo.org/records/18421797">Anatomy of the Spectre Tiling</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A400810 David Smith, Joseph Samuel Myers, Craig S. Kaplan, and Chaim Goodman-Strauss, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17743">A chiral aperiodic monotile</a>, arXiv:2305.17743 [math.CO], 2023-2024.
%H A400810 <a href="/index/Rec#order_03">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (3,15,1).
%F A400810 a(n) = 3*a(n-1) + 15*a(n-2) + a(n-3) for n > 3.
%F A400810 a(n) = a(n-1) + 3*A400811(n-1) for n > 1.
%F A400810 a(n) = 1 + 3*A397116(n-1) for n > 1.
%F A400810 G.f.: x*(1 + 4*x + x^2)/(1 - 3*x - 15*x^2 - x^3).
%e A400810 For n = 1, the Type C megastar is a single minor star triple: a(1) = 1.
%e A400810 For n = 2, it consists of the previous megastar a(1) = 1 and three Type A palindromes of size A400811(1) = 2, giving 1 + 3*2 = 7 star triples.
%e A400810 For n = 3, it consists of a(2) = 7 and three Type A palindromes of size A400811(2) = 10, giving 7 + 3*10 = 37 star triples.
%t A400810 LinearRecurrence[{3, 15, 1}, {1, 7, 37}, 23]
%o A400810 (PARI) Vec(x*(1 + 4*x + x^2)/(1 - 3*x - 15*x^2 - x^3) + O(x^24))
%Y A400810 Cf. A397115 (Family A), A397116 (Family C), A397117 (Family B), A397118 (Family D), A397119 (Family E).
%Y A400810 Cf. A397120 (Type A megastars), A400811 (Type A palindromes), A400812 (all star triples), A400821 (star triples in all Type C megastars), A400823 (number of Type C megastars).
%Y A400810 Cf. A015448.
